# https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ACE-NeuroTools
message: >-
  If you use ACE-NeuroTools in your research, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file. Until the companion paper is published, cite the software
  release directly.
type: software
authors:
  # Order matches `pyproject.toml [project.authors]`. Update both together.
  - given-names: Reed
    family-names: Pennock
    # email: TODO(humans)
    # orcid: TODO(humans)
    # affiliation: TODO(humans)
  - given-names: Luke
    family-names: Richards
    # email: TODO(humans)
    # orcid: TODO(humans)
    # affiliation: TODO(humans)
  - given-names: Eric
    family-names: Melonakos
    # email: TODO(humans)
    # orcid: TODO(humans)
    # affiliation: TODO(humans)
abstract: >-
  ACE-NeuroTools (Analysis of Calcium Imaging and Electrophysiology) is an
  open-source Python package providing integrated pipelines for one-photon
  (miniscope) calcium imaging, extracellular electrophysiology, and the
  multimodal alignment between them. It bundles motion correction, CNMF-E
  source extraction, calcium-event inference, ephys signal conditioning,
  artifact suppression, phase computation, and TTL-based cross-modal
  alignment behind a small set of pipeline objects driven by per-experiment
  CSV metadata.
keywords:
  - neuroscience
  - calcium-imaging
  - electrophysiology
  - miniscope
  - cnmfe
  - signal-processing
  - data-analysis
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: 'https://github.com/emelon8/experiment_analysis'
url: 'https://aceneurotools.readthedocs.io/en/latest/'  # TODO(humans): confirm RTD subdomain
version: 0.1.0
# Mint a Zenodo (or institutional) DOI when tagging the next release and
# paste the concept-DOI here. The version DOI is what most journals want;
# Zenodo issues both a concept-DOI (all-versions) and a version-DOI per tag.
